{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "project-useromd-gaps-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.60: `project-useromd-gaps`, a PROJECT-domain run whose user states operating modes that leave GAPS, computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE plus its PROJECT input database (`inputs/washtenaw-project-useromd-gaps.esm`). It selects source types 21 and 32 (gasoline, which MOVES widens to four fuels each), road types 4 and 5, running CO and Total Energy, brake wear and tire wear (PM10 and PM2.5).\n\nWHAT IT EXERCISES, behind the input opModeDistribution (`omd_*`): on link 1 the user states running CO, so LinkOperatingModeDistributionGenerator skips the link (java:330) and every running and brake-wear pollutant-process there is weighted by the user's rows ALONE -- running Total Energy has none and MOVES writes no row for it on link 1, and the trucks' brake wear has none and MOVES writes none either (`omd_userGap`, `rt_hasLinkModes`); the cars' brake wear is the user's four modes, mode 501 at its own rate. On link 2 the user states brake wear only: the generator runs, and its tempExistingOpMode anti-join (java:836-860) keeps the user's brake rows over its own (`omd_userGoverned`). Tire wear's project generator writes its mode from the link's speed and never reads opModeDistribution, so the user's mode-416 row on link 1 changes nothing. Before the port the model refused the run (`run_domainUnported` 27: `run_userLinkModeRows` 11, `run_userLinkGaps` 10, and 6 start-mode `sod_projectConflicts` it counted at the user's running and brake modes) and, read anyway, weighted the cars' brake wear by the generator (0.48 and 1.10 of MOVES on links 1 and 2, the trucks' 2.2-2.4 on link 2) and computed 494 rows MOVES does not write (running Total Energy on link 1 and the trucks' brake wear there).\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 2468. `run_domainUnported` is 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "project-domain"
    ]
  },
